Parallel trimming patch for Rowan (frozen files: NOT applied).   git apply Testing/notes/trim_parallel.patch
Made against speed/join 0221a57 (festive-fermi 050ef82 + speed/join). Touches Spec/Fastq.lean, Spec/Shim.lean, their copies
Proofs/Fastq.lean and Main.lean, and Proofs/TrimRecord.lean (new theorem trimChunk_eq). After applying, regenerate the checksum:
  shasum -a 256 Spec/Alignment.lean Spec/Mapping.lean Spec/Aligner.lean Spec/Shim.lean > Spec/FROZEN.sha256
(the regeneration is not in the patch).
- readChunk pushes (record1, record2) untrimmed.
- trimChunk chunk parts: the chunk is cut into `parts` slices of ceil(size / parts) pairs; each slice is trimmed
  (trimRecord on both mates) in its own dedicated Task; the slices are concatenated in order. It is self-contained
  (Spec/Fastq.lean does not import the mapper). It has ParMap.parMap's batch structure, so
  trimChunk_eq : trimChunk chunk parts = chunk.map (trim both) holds by rfl after ParMap.parMap_eq_map
  (standard axioms).
- Shim / Main: both reading tasks become IO.asTask (do let raw <- Spec.readChunk reads1 reads2 20000; return Spec.trimChunk raw 16).
On top of shim_speed.patch: apply shim_speed first, then this one with `git apply --3way`. One conflict in
Proofs/TrimRecord.lean at the end of the file: drop the `#print axioms Spec.trimRecord_quality_bytes` line
(shim_speed removes that theorem) and keep trimChunk_eq.
Verification is in Testing/notes/TRIM_PARALLEL.md.

